---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

const title = 'Case Report: Lumbar Disc Herniation Rehab | Boston MA';
const description = 'Complete 8-week clinical case documentation of an L4-L5 disc protrusion with radicular pain resolved through flexion-distraction and reformer pilates.';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: `${base}/` },
  { name: 'Case Studies', url: `${base}/case-studies/` },
  { name: 'L4-L5 Disc Herniation', url: `${base}/case-studies/spinal-decompression-lumbar-herniation/` }
];

const articleSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'MedicalScholarlyArticle',
  headline: 'Clinical Management of L4-L5 Lumbar Disc Extrusion Utilizing Cox Flexion-Distraction and Reformer Pilates',
  author: {
    '@type': 'Person',
    name: 'Dr. Benjamin Williams, DC'
  },
  publisher: {
    '@type': 'MedicalBusiness',
    name: 'ChiroHaven Spine & Physical Therapy'
  },
  datePublished: '2024-10-15',
  description: 'Detailed retrospective clinical case study describing diagnosis, intervention, and 6-month follow-up for lumbar radiculopathy.'
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} extraSchema={articleSchema}>
  <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container article-container">
      <div class="article-header">
        <p class="section-eyebrow">Retrospective Clinical Report</p>
        <h1>Non-Surgical Resolution of Lumbar L4-L5 Disc Herniation with Radiculopathy</h1>
        <div class="article-byline">
          <span><strong>Author:</strong> Dr. Benjamin Williams, DC, Clinic Director</span>
          <span><strong>Published:</strong> October 2024</span>
          <span><strong>Peer Review:</strong> Internal Clinical Conference</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="article-body">
        <div class="article-lead-box">
          <h2>Abstract & Executive Summary</h2>
          <p>
            A 42-year-old software executive presented with severe left-sided lower back and radicular pain descending past the knee into the lateral foot. MRI examination confirmed an 8mm postero-lateral disc extrusion at L4-L5 abutting the exiting L5 nerve root. Through an integrated 8-week conservative protocol combining motorized Cox flexion-distraction spinal decompression, instrumented myofascial release, and progressive clinical reformer stabilization, the patient achieved complete symptom abolition and returned to unrestricted functional activity without surgical intervention.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2>1. Initial Patient Presentation & History</h2>
        <p>
          The patient reported a 6-month history of mild intermittent back stiffness exacerbated by long desk working hours. Two weeks prior to initial consultation, a sudden lifting and twisting event produced acute lower back spasms followed by excruciating shooting pain down the posterior-lateral aspect of the left lower extremity.
        </p>
        <ul role="list">
          <li><strong>Visual Analogue Scale (VAS):</strong> 8/10 at rest, 10/10 during sit-to-stand transitions.</li>
          <li><strong>Oswestry Disability Index (ODI):</strong> 62% (Severe functional disability).</li>
          <li><strong>Neurological Screening:</strong> Diminished left Achilles reflex (1+ vs 2+ right); hypoesthesia over the L5 dermatome. Straight Leg Raise (SLR) positive on the left at 25 degrees.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. Clinical Diagnosis & Imaging Confirmation</h2>
        <p>
          Lumbar spine MRI without contrast revealed well-preserved disc height at L1-L3, with moderate disc desiccation at L4-L5 accompanied by an 8.2mm subligamentous disc extrusion producing significant left lateral recess stenosis and displacement of the left L5 nerve root.
        </p>

        <h2>3. 8-Week Multi-Disciplinary Intervention Protocol</h2>
        <p>Care was structured into three distinct clinical phases. Select any phase to review mechanical interventions and physiological adaptation:</p>

        <div class="phase-interactive-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Clinical rehabilitation phases">
          <button type="button" class="phase-tab active" data-phase="1" role="tab" aria-selected="true" id="tab-phase-1" aria-controls="panel-phase-1">
            <span class="tab-badge">Phase 1</span>
            <span class="tab-title">Weeks 1–2: Decompression</span>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="phase-tab" data-phase="2" role="tab" aria-selected="false" id="tab-phase-2" aria-controls="panel-phase-2">
            <span class="tab-badge">Phase 2</span>
            <span class="tab-title">Weeks 3–5: Core Retraining</span>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="phase-tab" data-phase="3" role="tab" aria-selected="false" id="tab-phase-3" aria-controls="panel-phase-3">
            <span class="tab-badge">Phase 3</span>
            <span class="tab-title">Weeks 6–8: Functional Return</span>
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="phase-panels-wrap">
          <div class="phase-card active" id="panel-phase-1" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-phase-1">
            <h3>Phase I: Acute Decompression & Pain Centralization (Weeks 1–2)</h3>
            <p>
              <strong>Clinical Objective:</strong> Retract extruded disc fragment from L5 nerve root and abolish radiating leg pain.<br />
              <strong>Treatment Frequency:</strong> 3 sessions per week.<br />
              <strong>Modalities:</strong> Motorized Cox Technic flexion-distraction table utilizing automated rhythmic lumbar traction to widen intervertebral foramina by 28% and decrease intradiscal pressures. Gentle cryotherapy and passive supine positioning with 90/90 knee flexion.
            </p>
            <div class="phase-stat-badge">Measured VAS: Dropped from 8.5/10 to 5.0/10</div>
          </div>

          <div class="phase-card" id="panel-phase-2" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-phase-2" hidden>
            <h3>Phase II: Core Neuromuscular Re-Education (Weeks 3–5)</h3>
            <p>
              <strong>Clinical Objective:</strong> Retrain deep stabilizing musculature (multifidus & transversus abdominis) to protect disc annulus.<br />
              <strong>Treatment Frequency:</strong> 2 sessions per week.<br />
              <strong>Modalities:</strong> Transition to active rehabilitation on the clinical reformer. Focus on diaphragmatic breath retraining, isometric transversus abdominis activation without spinal flexion, and active hamstring neural mobilization glides.
            </p>
            <div class="phase-stat-badge">Measured VAS: Dropped to 3.0/10 • Straight Leg Raise: 58°</div>
          </div>

          <div class="phase-card" id="panel-phase-3" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-phase-3" hidden>
            <h3>Phase III: Functional Loading & Workstation Ergonomics (Weeks 6–8)</h3>
            <p>
              <strong>Clinical Objective:</strong> Restore full rotational capacity, return to sports conditioning, and workplace desk resilience.<br />
              <strong>Treatment Frequency:</strong> 1 session per week.<br />
              <strong>Modalities:</strong> Progressive resistance hip hinge mechanics, single-leg stance balance drills, dead bug variations on reformer, and ergonomic workstation setup (alternating sit-stand protocol).
            </p>
            <div class="phase-stat-badge">Discharge VAS: 0.5/10 • ODI: 4% (Complete recovery)</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2>4. Measured Objective Outcomes</h2>
        <div class="data-table-wrapper" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Clinical outcome metrics table">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Clinical Metric</th>
                <th scope="col">Baseline (Day 1)</th>
                <th scope="col">Week 4 (Mid-Care)</th>
                <th scope="col">Week 8 (Discharge)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">VAS Pain Rating (0–10)</th>
                <td>8.5 / 10</td>
                <td>3.0 / 10</td>
                <td><strong>0.5 / 10</strong></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Oswestry Disability Index (ODI)</th>
                <td>62% (Severe)</td>
                <td>24% (Moderate)</td>
                <td><strong>4% (Minimal)</strong></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Straight Leg Raise Angle</th>
                <td>25° (Left side positive)</td>
                <td>58° (Slight tightness)</td>
                <td><strong>82° (Normal / Negative)</strong></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">L5 Dermatome Sensation</th>
                <td>Hypoesthesia present</td>
                <td>Partial sensation return</td>
                <td><strong>Full normal sensation</strong></td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h2>5. 6-Month Long-Term Follow-Up</h2>
        <p>
          At 6 months post-discharge, the patient reported maintaining their 15-minute daily home core stabilization routine. The patient has successfully resumed running 12 to 15 miles per week and reports zero recurrence of radicular leg symptoms.
        </p>

        <div class="article-footer-cta">
          <h3>Experiencing Disc or Sciatic Nerve Symptoms?</h3>
          <p>Schedule a comprehensive consultation to determine if you are a candidate for non-surgical spinal decompression.</p>
          <a href={`${base}/contact/`} class="btn btn-primary">
            Request Spinal Evaluation
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<script is:inline>
  (function() {
    const tabs = document.querySelectorAll('.phase-tab');
    const panels = document.querySelectorAll('.phase-card');

    tabs.forEach((tab) => {
      tab.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const pNum = tab.getAttribute('data-phase');

        tabs.forEach((t) => {
          t.classList.remove('active');
          t.setAttribute('aria-selected', 'false');
        });
        tab.classList.add('active');
        tab.setAttribute('aria-selected', 'true');

        panels.forEach((p) => {
          if (p.id === `panel-phase-${pNum}`) {
            p.hidden = false;
            p.classList.add('active');
          } else {
            p.hidden = true;
            p.classList.remove('active');
          }
        });
      });
    });
  })();
</script>

<style>
  .article-container {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .article-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .article-byline {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .article-lead-box {
    background: var(--color-surface-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-primary);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .article-lead-box h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .article-body h2 {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .article-body ul {
    margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .phase-interactive-tabs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 1.25rem;
  }

  .phase-tab {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 2px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    text-align: left;
    transition: background-color var(--transition-fast), border-color var(--transition-fast), transform var(--transition-fast);
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 180px;
  }

  .phase-tab:hover {
    background: var(--color-surface-subtle);
    border-color: var(--color-border-strong);
  }

  .phase-tab.active {
    background: #0c221f;
    border-color: #0c221f;
    color: #ffffff;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(12, 34, 31, 0.15);
  }

  .tab-badge {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }

  .phase-tab.active .tab-badge {
    color: #8be2c7;
  }

  .tab-title {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .phase-stat-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    background: #e6ede9;
    color: #12332c;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    padding: 0.35rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .phase-card {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .phase-card.active {
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-primary);
  }

  .phase-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .article-footer-cta {
    background: var(--color-surface-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 2rem;
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
  }

  .article-footer-cta h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .article-footer-cta p {
    margin: 0 auto 1.5rem;
  }
</style>

